x['notes']=r'''The expectation \(\mathbb E_x[f(B_t)\exp(-\int_0^tV(B_s)ds)]\) is the evolution operator for \(-\tfrac12\Delta+V\).'''
x['statement']=r'''For Brownian motion with generator \(\tfrac12\Delta\) and bounded real V, \(e^{-tH}f(x)=\mathbb E_x[f(B_t)\exp(-\int_0^tV(B_s)ds)]\), where \(H=-\tfrac12\Delta+V\). The equality extends to suitable Kato-class potentials, with the operator defined by its closed semibounded quadratic form. The bounded-potential version already makes the displayed formula precise.'''
x['fate']=r'''This is the classical Feynman--Kac formula; \citet[formula (A26), Theorem A.2.7]{simon1982semigroups} treats it systematically. The later survey is a verification source, not a post-1980 priority claim.'''
x['present_status']=DATE+'the formula is established with the specified operator sign and potential hypotheses.'
item(495,'P000928','claim','Large-time logarithmic growth and the bottom of the spectrum',r'''The logarithmic expectation divided by t is asserted to approach \(\pm\lambda_1\).''',r'''On a compact connected Riemannian manifold, for continuous real V and \(H=-\tfrac12\Delta+V\), the positive ground state gives \(\lim_{t\to\infty}t^{-1}\log\mathbb E_x\exp(-\int_0^tV(B_s)ds)=-\lambda_0(H)\). A noncompact version needs additional potential, spectral and pointwise-growth hypotheses; the compact formulation is an explicit safe specialization, not a claim that the notes stated compactness.''','E',r'''The spectral-semigroup mechanism is classical; compare \citet[\S B.5]{simon1982semigroups}. The sign follows from \(e^{-tH}\), and is not an independent plus-or-minus choice.''','the compact-case limit holds. The source’s unspecified noncompact generality is not certified.',['simon1982semigroups'],reconstruction='Compactness and connectedness are supplied as an explicit sufficient setting; no claim is made that they were present in the notebook.',literal='correct with missing hypotheses',match='partial',area='Spectral theory and probability')

